    "c2": {
      "anchor": "q8",
      "kind": "item",
      "label": "What if a draw or getter calls something slow?",
      "excerpt": "What if a draw or getter calls something slow?",
      "text": "Would this be simpler if we ditched the JS output target and just supported TS and Python?",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-10-31T04:09:45.940Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "ts/lib keeps only the classes and never draws, so a waiting getter there has no draw to worry about.",
      "offset": 5399,
      "edited": "2026-10-31T04:10:06.290Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-10-31T04:11:37.435Z",
          "html": "<p>No:  the waiting work sits below the writers, TypeScript is built on the JavaScript writer, and JavaScript is what the editor and runners run.  Python and <code>ts/lib</code> would still need their own answer.  The full reply is in Q8.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
